\check Apply Paragraph Markers 2026 [CAN CHANGE TEXT]
\description Copy paragraph and poetry markers (default: \p \q1 \q2) from a Model text onto the selected books of this project, matched up verse by verse.\n\nThe Model text supplies the markers (e.g. a project that already has \p/\q1/\q2 in place); this project supplies the base text that receives them. If the Output Project is the same as this project, the changes are made "in place".\n\nA marker already present immediately before a verse in this project is left alone, not duplicated. Poetry/paragraph marker lines that continue mid-verse (a marker followed by ordinary text, not by a \v) are not copied, since there is no way to place them at the right word - only markers that directly precede a \v marker in the Model text are transferred.\n\nVerses that exist in the Model text but not in this project are listed in the results with a note that the marker for that verse could not be copied.\n\nSet "Remove existing paragraph markers first" to Y to strip this project's own markers before copying, rather than merging with what's already there - useful when the existing markers are wrong or inconsistent and you want a clean re-copy from the Model text instead.

\subMenu Unsupported

# Run a python script
\script ApplyParagraphMarkers2026.py
\programToRun Python

# Prompt user for which books to process
\books

# The check will read the text itself
\noText
\outputProject

\optionName ModelText
\optionLocalizedName Model text (has the markers)
\optionDescription Enter the short name of the project that already has the paragraph/poetry markers you want to copy.
\optionListAllTexts

\optionName MarkersToCopy
\optionLocalizedName Markers to copy
\optionDescription Space-separated list of USFM markers to copy from the Model text. Type ONE backslash before each marker, e.g. \p \q1 \q2 - not two. Leave blank to use the default.
\optionDefault \p \q1 \q2

\optionName ClearExistingMarkers
\optionLocalizedName Remove existing paragraph markers first
\optionDescription Enter Y to strip every marker listed above (wherever it occurs, not just before a verse) out of this project before copying fresh ones from the Model text. Enter N to leave existing markers alone and only add ones that are missing.
\optionDefault N

# Output of this check is to go to the list window
\toList

# This file is encoded using utf-8
\utf8

#\helpFile SampleScript.rtf

